              %li
                %a{:href => "#examples"} Examples
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Uniform convergence spaces are simultaneously a generalisation of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uniform+spaces"} uniform spaces
            and a specialisation with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extra+structure"} extra structure
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convergence+spaces"} convergence spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Unif
                  %mo →
                  %mi Unif
                  %mi Conv
                  %mo →
                  %mi Conv
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Unif \to Unif Conv \to Conv ,
          %p
            both
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/faithful+functor"} faithful
            and with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Unif
                  %mo →
                  %mi Unif
                  %mi Conv
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Unif \to Unif Conv
            also
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+functor"} full
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Unif
                  %mi Conv
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Unif Conv
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Unif
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Unif
            to be the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uniformly+continuous+maps"} uniformly continuous maps
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Conv
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Conv
            must use the
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+maps"} continuous maps
          %h2#motivation Motivation
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uniform+property"} uniform properties
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+space"} metric space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            are determined entirely by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
            between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinite+sequences"} infinite sequences
            through which sequences
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            are related iff the distance between them tends to zero:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munder
                    %mi lim
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo →
                      %mn ∞
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lim_{n \to \infty} {\|a_n - b_n\|} = 0 .
          %p
            An analogous result holds for a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uniform+space"} uniform space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            if one generalises from sequences to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nets"} nets
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+spaces"} metric spaces
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
            without
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+countable+choice"} weak countable choice
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+set"} directed set
            as
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain"} domain
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                  %mo ,
                  %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m, n \to \infty
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mi m
                      %mo −
                      %msub
                        %mi b
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|a_m - b_n\|}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+equivalence+relation"} partial equivalence relation
            that applies only to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+sequences"} Cauchy sequences
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+structure"} Cauchy structure
            and not the entire
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uniform+structure"} uniform structure
          %p
            Rather than speak of two nets with the same domain, let us speak equivalently of a single net in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+square"} cartesian square
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/size+issue"} small
            definition, let us speak of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filter"} filter
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            will be a collection of filters on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times X
            = succeed ")," do
              %span.newWikiWord
                metrizable uniform space
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/metrizable+uniform+space"} ?
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abstract+set"} abstract set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            be a collection of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filters"} filters
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+square"} cartesian square
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times X
            = succeed "." do
              %strong asymptotic filters
          %p
            A collection that satisfies all of (1–6) below is a
            = succeed "." do
              %strong uniform convergence structure
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base"} base
            for a uniform convergence structure; if it satisfies at least (4–6), then it is a
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subbase"} subbase
            for a uniform convergence structure. That said, we could start with a perfectly arbitrary collection and generate a subbase, then a base, then an entire structure.
          %p
            If we use (6′) instead of (6), then this is a
            = succeed "." do
              %strong pointwise uniform convergence structure
            = succeed "." do
              %strong quasiuniform convergence structure
          %p
            A (pointwise) (quasi)-
            %strong uniform convergence space
            is a set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            equipped with such a structure.
          %p Here are the relevant properties:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %em> Isotone
                \: If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \subseteq G
                (as filters on
                = succeed ")" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ×
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times X
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                is asymptotic, then
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                is asymptotic.
            %li
              %p
                %em> Proper
                \: There is an asymptotic filter. If (1) also holds, then we may equivalently say that the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/improper+filter"} improper filter
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ×
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times X
                is asymptotic. This is automatic if (6) holds but is independent of the other conditions; it
                %em almost
                follows from (6′), but only if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                is
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+set"} inhabited
            %li
              %p
                %em> Filtered
                \: If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                are asymptotic filters, then there is an asymptotic filter contained in both
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersection"} intersection
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo ∩
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \cap G
                is asymptotic.
            %li
              %p
                %em> Symmetric
                \: If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                is an asymptotic filter, then there is an asymptotic filter
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                with the property that, whenever
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \in G
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+relation"} inverse
                (as a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/binary+relation"} binary relation
                on
                = succeed ")" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi R
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R^{-1}
                belongs to
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msup
                        %mi R
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi R
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{ R^{-1} \;|\; R \in F \}
                is asymptotic.
            %li
              %p
                %em> Transitive
                \: If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                are asymptotic filters, then there is an asymptotic filter
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
                with the property that, whenever
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi H
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \in H
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+number"} natural number
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tuple"} tuple
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi S
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi …
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi S
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∈
                        %msup
                          %mi F
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (S_1, \ldots, S_n) \in F^n
                = succeed "-tuple" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi G
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (T_1, \ldots, T_n) \in G^n
                such that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo ⊇
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ∘
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∩
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo ∩
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mi n
                      %mo ∘
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \supseteq (S_1 \circ T_1) \cap \cdots \cap (S_n \circ T_n)
                (where
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∘
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \circ
                indicates
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/binary+relations"} binary relations
                on
                = succeed ")." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi S
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi T
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi S
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi F
                      %mo ,
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi T
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{ S \circ T \;|\; S \in F,\; T \in G \}
                is asymptotic.
            %li
              %p
                %em> Reflexive
                \: There is an asymptotic filter
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                with the property that each
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \in F
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflexive+relation"} reflexive
                as a binary relation on
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p Although (6) as given here is in the original definition and is the proper nullary analogue of the binary (5), a weaker version is now more popular:
          %ul
            %li
              (6′).
              = succeed ":" do
                %em Pointwise reflexive
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              with the property that each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \in F
              satisfies
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a,a) \in R
              (so that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is reflexive at
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              (which is a filter, indeed the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+ultrafilter"} principal ultrafilter
              at
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a,a)
          %p
            One reason for this is apparently to render the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of uniform convergence spaces
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian closed
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            satisfying (6) such that the set of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uniformly+continuous+maps"} uniformly continuous maps
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            can be given only a pointwise uniform convergence structure.
          %p
            For the purposes of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
          %ul
            %li
              (7).
              = succeed ":" do
                %em Comparison
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              is an asymptotic filter, then there is an asymptotic filter
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              with the property that, whenever
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \in G
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \in F
              such that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ¬
                      %mi R
                      %mo ∪
                      %mi S
                      %mo =
                      %mi X
                      %mo ×
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg{R} \cup S = X \times X
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excluded+middle"} excluded middle
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              to be
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              itself (and take
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              to be
              = succeed ")," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+mathematics"} classical mathematics
          %p
            A (pointwise) (quasi)-uniform convergence structure/space that satisfies (7) may be called (quasi)-
            %strong uniformly regular space|uniformly regular
            (although ‘(quasi)-uniformly
            = succeed "\u2019" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+decomposable+space"} locally decomposable
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+space"} regular
          %p
            It is traditional to consider only
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+filter"} proper
            asymptotic filters (or equivalently to consider only asymptotic
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nets"} nets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersection"} meets
            each element of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+set"} inhabited
          %p
            The conditions (1,2,3,4,5,6,7) correspond respectively to the conditions (6,4,5,2,3,1,0) at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uniform+space"} uniform space
            (as of 2013-02-22, in case the latter are ever renumbered). However, (6′) has no direct analogue.
          %h2#terminology_warning Terminology warning
          %p
            Among the terms defined (in boldface) above, I (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Toby+Bartels"}> Toby Bartels
            ) invented ‘asymptotic filter’ and those involving ‘pointwise’ and ‘quasi‑’, because no appropriate terms appeared in the reference that I used. Possibly other terms appear in the literature (besides the fact that ‘pointwise’ may simply be left out). That said, my use of ‘quasi‑’ follows
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasimetric"} quasimetric
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasiuniform+space"} quasiuniform space
            %span.newWikiWord
              asymptotic function
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/asymptotic+function"} ?
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complexity+theory"} complexity theory
            (which is weaker, and in fact says that functions are asymptotic when their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/logarithms"} logarithms
            are asymptotic in our sense), although it matches the meaning of
            %span.newWikiWord
              asymptote
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/asymptote"} ?
            in elementary
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analytic+geometry"} analytic geometry
          %h2#subsidiary_concepts Subsidiary concepts
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            be pointwise uniform convergence spaces. A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            from
