            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uniform+space"} uniform space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/net"} net
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times X
            be
            %em asymptotic
            if, when viewed as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pairing"} pair
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a,b)
            of nets (with common domain) in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munder
                    %mi lim
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo →
                      %mn ∞
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mi n
                  %msubsup
                    %mi b
                    %mi n
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lim_{n \to \infty} a_n b_n^{-1} = 1
          %p (on one side) or
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munder
                    %mi lim
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo →
                      %mn ∞
                  %msubsup
                    %mi a
                    %mi n
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lim_{n \to \infty} a_n^{-1} b_n = 1
          %p
            (on the other side). The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/eventuality+filters"} eventuality filters
            of the asymptotic nets in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times X
            form a base for a uniform convergence structure; indeed, they are precisely the proper asymptotic filters. The convergence structure induced by this uniform convergence structure agrees with the original convergence structure on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            (which must be reciprocal, for essentially the same reason that the topology of a topological group must be). Probably one can get a quasiuniform convergence structure or four out of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid+object"} monoid object
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Conv
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Conv
          %h2#references References
          %p Pages 72–76 (in Part I) in
          %ul
            %li
              Jan Harm van der Walt (2009);
              %em Generalized solutions of systems of nonlinear partial differential equations
              (PhD thesis);
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://upetd.up.ac.za/thesis/available/etd-05242009-122628/"} web
          %p (This dissertation is not really about uniform convergence spaces, but it has the advantage of being free online.)
